---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "APR When Fees Are Financed";
const description =
  "Financed fees change APR and total cost. Learn how to compare financed vs paid-upfront fees. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-08";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/apr-when-fees-are-financed" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Financed fees</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>APR when fees are financed</h1>
    <p>
      Paying fees upfront lowers the net amount you receive, while financing fees raises the balance. This guide shows
      how each option affects APR and total dollars paid.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-with-origination-fee">APR with origination fee</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">APR comparison inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount and term (keep them constant across offers).</li>
      <li>Nominal rate vs APR and which fees are included.</li>
      <li>Upfront fees paid in cash vs financed.</li>
      <li>Expected time horizon before refinance or payoff.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Two ways fees show up</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li><strong>Paid upfront:</strong> lower net amount received.</li>
      <li><strong>Financed:</strong> higher balance and more interest over time.</li>
      <li>APR can differ even if the rate is the same.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to compare</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Run the APR calculator with fees paid upfront.</li>
      <li>Run it again with fees financed (add to the loan amount).</li>
      <li>Compare APR and total dollars paid over your horizon.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Inputs to confirm</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Exact fee totals and which fees are financeable.</li>
      <li>Cash-to-close budget for upfront fees.</li>
      <li>Whether fees increase the loan amount or are paid separately.</li>
      <li>Expected payoff horizon for total cost comparison.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare total dollars paid for both fee options.</li>
      <li>Confirm the same term and rate in each scenario.</li>
      <li>Re-run if you change the loan amount or fees.</li>
      <li>Choose the option that fits cash flow and horizon.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Scenario notes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare a short horizon if you plan to refinance soon.</li>
      <li>Use the same discount points and credits in both runs.</li>
      <li>Check if rolling fees affects loan-to-value limits.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Comparing APRs without matching the same term.</li>
      <li>Ignoring cash-to-close when choosing the fee option.</li>
      <li>Assuming financed fees are always worse.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-vs-interest-rate">Interest rate vs APR</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits">Points vs credits</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Does financing fees always raise APR?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      It often does, but the effect depends on term, rate, and fee size. Compare both options.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Which option is better for short horizons?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      It depends on cash flow. Compare total dollars paid over your expected horizon.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">Run APR comparisons</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-with-origination-fee">APR with origination fee</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-08</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>





